      "interpretation": "FAIL-WITH-FINDING (R7.3): only 1 distinct dominant point(s) on the frontier. Under the tug-of-war dynamics the stage-aware proportional oracle (recommended_action) attains perfect security (security_gain=1.0) at near-zero availability cost, strictly dominating always_block (which also prevents 100% but at unit availability cost) and every interior learned policy. The security-availability trade-off therefore collapses to a single dominant operating point *given perfect stage perception*; the interior placement of the RL agents quantifies the cost of partial observability (POMDP), not a genuine multi-point frontier."
    }
